cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it. The theoretical model remains under active review by our team of collaborators and should be considered provisional."
type: software
title: "NODOX"
abstract: >-
  NODOX is an explainable, evidence-aware bioinformatics platform for
  prioritizing bacterial therapeutic-target hypotheses through Functional Node
  Theory, explicit provenance, evidence-confidence assessment, and evolutionary
  escape-risk analysis. The theoretical model underlying NODOX remains under
  active review by our team of collaborators; its assumptions, variables, and
  interpretation are provisional and may change as that review progresses.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-20"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DANISRAELZ/NODOX"
url: "https://github.com/DANISRAELZ/NODOX"
authors:
  - given-names: "Dan Israel"
    family-names: "Zavala Vargas"
keywords:
  - functional nodes
  - therapeutic prioritization
  - computational biology
  - evidence integration
  - reproducible workflow
  - user curated evidence
